Merged categories laid out as Xcode 27.0's ld lays them out (B-193, docs/formats/build.md "Objective-C references,
archive members and hints in the linked image"): categories merged into one keep the first category's body, name and
list slot; merging into a class rewrites only the lists the categories add to; the merged lists are named
<prefix><class>(<categories>) with __OBJC_$_INSTANCE_METHODS_, __OBJC_$_CLASS_METHODS_ and __OBJC_CLASS_PROTOCOLS_$_,
the property lists without a symbol. __objc_methlist holds the live method lists of classes, categories and protocols,
ordered by their symbols' names, each at a multiple of 8 bytes. lld wrote a new category named "A|B", rewrote every
list of the class, named the lists __OBJC_$_INSTANCE_METHODS_(C) and __OBJC_$_CATEGORY_CLASS_METHODS_..., left the
protocols' lists in __objc_const, ended merged protocol lists with a null pointer and kept the replaced lists, in
input order.
